text:
harper: Heads-up: we're noticing a few flagged examples where streaming calls still use the old v1 framing and the SDK helper param `streaming=true`. Need a short migration note for streaming changes in the v1 -> v2 migration guide.

gio: can you summarize the behavior change? I saw some customers hit JSON parse errors with the new runtime.

harper: summary: v1 returned newline-delimited JSON chunks and required client-side aggregation. v2 uses HTTP SSE-ish framing and top-level `chunk` objects; SDKs now expose `client.streamResponses()` instead of `client.invoke({streaming:true})`.

anika: thanks. so we need three things: docs snippet replacements, a short explanation of the framing diff (with example decoder), and a smoke test in examples.

harper: exactly. propose adding a small snippet in the migration guide labeled "Streaming migration (quick)" showing old vs new and a tiny JS decoder. Also note the SDK rename and examples for Python and Go.

gio: example decoder please — that'll help integrators. also call out common error: `Unexpected token` when reading legacy NDJSON consumer.

harper: adding sample JS decoder to the PR:
```js
// old v1 NDJSON style (pseudo)
// data: {chunk: '...', done: false}
const reader = response.body.getReader()
let buf = ''
while(true){
  const {value, done} = await reader.read()
  if(done) break
  buf += new TextDecoder().decode(value)
  const parts = buf.split('\n')
  buf = parts.pop() // incomplete
  for(const p of parts){
    const obj = JSON.parse(p)
    handleChunk(obj)
  }
}

// new v2 SSE-like framing example (SDK exposes streamResponses)
const stream = client.streamResponses({model:'chat-v2', input:'hi'})
for await (const event of stream) {
  if(event.type === 'delta') processDelta(event.delta)
  if(event.type === 'done') finalize()
}
```

anika: add this to migration guide and a short note for SDK owners: change surface from `invoke({streaming:true})` to `streamResponses()` and remove client.v1 shims.

docs-ci: added lint rule `no-v1-streaming` to docs CI and a draft PR #1601. The linter flags `streaming:true` and `/v1/stream`.

gio: also include a small Python example, since folks use iterator patterns there:
```py
# old
resp = client.invoke(model='chat-v1', streaming=True, input='hi')
for chunk in resp:
    print(chunk)

# new
for event in client.stream_responses(model='chat-v2', input='hi'):
    if event['type'] == 'delta': print(event['delta'])
```

harper: one more: document a fallback pattern for older runtimes during the transition: show how to wrap old NDJSON consumers with a shim that converts NDJSON -> SSE-like events. We'll include the shim code in an appendix.

anika: and call out embed alias swaps in same migration page (embed-v1-small -> embed-lite-v2) and remind users to re-index if dims change. Add note: streaming embedding generation will now return a single embed payload instead of incremental partial vectors.

gio: timeline? we should coordinate with SDK patches so docs publish around the same time.

harper: plan: publish streaming migration note Tue EOD, enable advisory lint Wed, SDK patch releases Wed-Fri with streamResponses/stream_responses implemented, hard lint block after 5 days. I'll open the main PR and tag SDK leads.

docs-ci: linked PR #1602 to issue #601 and added reviewers @anika @gio @harper

gio: I'll run a grep for `streaming:true|stream_responses|streamResponses|v1/stream` across examples and open fixes. Tagging infra to help with archived content.

harper: great. Please also add a one-line blurb for #announcements and the Integrations Slack so customers see the change window.

anika: will draft the announcement: 2 lines + link to streaming migration section + link to SDK patch notes.

harper: thanks team  ping here when PRs land and I'll shepherd the publish steps.
